  "conditioning_scope_and_limitations": "These percentile intervals summarize uncertainty arising strictly from resampling held-out observations for fixed, already-fitted model artifacts. They do NOT include uncertainty from retraining on a new training set, changing the synthetic data-generation process, temporal distribution shifts, or real-world population changes. Paired intervals use shared observation indices, preserving observation-level covariance across model predictions. An interval crossing zero does not establish that two models are equivalent, and an interval excluding zero is not by itself proof of business significance or deployment readiness.",
